{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4BlockMap211","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4BlockMap211","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4AlgebraLaws","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4BlockRep","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.H4A.blockRep211","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.H4A.blockRep211","kind":"def","line":508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4BlockMap211.lean#L508-L536","doc":"**The $(2,1,1)$ block representation (sorry-free).**  The algebra\nhomomorphism `H₄(q) →ₐ M_3(K)` induced by the explicit-entry block map;\nwith the two characters and the sibling blocks this is the block *data*\nof $H_4(q) \\cong K \\times K \\times M_2 \\times M_3 \\times M_3$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.blockOf211_mulNF₄","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.blockOf211_mulNF₄","kind":"theorem","line":489,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4BlockMap211.lean#L489-L503","doc":"**Multiplicativity of the $(2,1,1)$ block map on the full NF product\n(sorry-free)** — expand along the right basis, peel every word composite\nwith the three intertwiners (both for general `u` and for `u = γ`, which\nrecovers the word-product decomposition of the explicit entries), and\ncollect with associativity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.blockOf211_mulσ₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.blockOf211_mulσ₂","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4BlockMap211.lean#L239-L318","doc":"The block map intertwines the right `σ₂`-action with right\nmultiplication by `S2_211` (9 scalar goals; each closed by\n`linear_combination` with the sympy-derived, exactly-verified SET-E\ncofactors — sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.blockOf211_mulσ₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.blockOf211_mulσ₁","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4BlockMap211.lean#L153-L236","doc":"The block map intertwines the right `σ₁`-action with right\nmultiplication by `S1_211` (9 scalar goals; each closed by\n`linear_combination` with the sympy-derived, exactly-verified SET-E\ncofactors — sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.blockOf211_mulσ₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.blockOf211_mulσ₀","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4BlockMap211.lean#L88-L150","doc":"The block map intertwines the right `σ₀`-action with right\nmultiplication by `S0_211` (9 scalar goals; each closed by\n`linear_combination` with the sympy-derived, exactly-verified SET-E\ncofactors — sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.blockOf211_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.blockOf211_unit","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4BlockMap211.lean#L80-L85","doc":"The unit $\\gamma$ maps to the identity matrix — column 0 of $A$ is the\nidentity block $(2,1,1)$-component (sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.blockOf211","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.blockOf211","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4BlockMap211.lean#L63-L77","doc":"The $(2,1,1)$ block map on NF coordinates, by **explicit entries**:\nrow $r$, column $c$ is the `rho211_{rc}` row of the verified 24×24\ncoordinate matrix $A$ applied to $v$ (inverse atoms kept separated:\nonly `q⁻¹`, `(q ^ 2 + 1)⁻¹`, `(q ^ 4 + q ^ 2 + 1)⁻¹`, `(q ^ 4 + 1)⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}